(1589860, 211942, 37234, '<td valign="top">I get the concept of life itself being all the riches you need, but I''m not quite certain I understand how the belt infers the same thing. In other words, it''s a great idea, but the photo doesn''t stand alone. You absolutely need both the title of the shot and the topic of the challenge, and even then the belt doesn''t really make sense. I hope you''re of the mind to take constructive criticism in the way it was meant - I''m not trying to offend you, here. I just don''t think your photo conveys as much meaning as the title does.</td>', 'I get the concept of life itself being all the riches you need, but I''m not quite certain I understand how the belt infers the same thing. In other words, it''s a great idea, but the photo doesn''t stand alone. You absolutely need both the title of the shot and the topic of the challenge, and even then the belt doesn''t really make sense. I hope you''re of the mind to take constructive criticism in the way it was meant - I''m not trying to offend you, here. I just don''t think your photo conveys as much meaning as the title does.', '2005-08-06 00:26:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1589864, 212136, 33560, '<td valign="top">My summer cottage.  You''ve found my summer cottage. And I had just about forgotten about it!  <br/> <br/>Curious.  I''ve seen so many photos of England in fog  and diffuse light that seeing a house like this in direct, undiffused light makes it seem somehow wrong - as if the house and its gardens had some how been transported for the day just to be photographed beneath the blazing north African skies.<br/> <br/>The sky seems just a tad too aqua or green. And so do the bricks.  Come to think of it, that lovely green hedge - I bet it is that color when the sky is cloudy but i''d not be surprised if it were considerably more yellow in bright light.<br/> <br/>Not sure how to make the composition better, but it somehow seems unbalanced.  If the photo is about the house, I''d like that to take up more space.  If it is about the grounds, I''d like their features to be more pronounced, more distinct.</td>', 'My summer cottage.  You''ve found my summer cottage. And I had just about forgotten about it!   Curious.  I''ve seen so many photos of England in fog  and diffuse light that seeing a house like this in direct, undiffused light makes it seem somehow wrong - as if the house and its gardens had some how been transported for the day just to be photographed beneath the blazing north African skies. The sky seems just a tad too aqua or green. And so do the bricks.  Come to think of it, that lovely green hedge - I bet it is that color when the sky is cloudy but i''d not be surprised if it were considerably more yellow in bright light. Not sure how to make the composition better, but it somehow seems unbalanced.  If the photo is about the house, I''d like that to take up more space.  If it is about the grounds, I''d like their features to be more pronounced, more distinct.', '2005-08-06 00:27:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1589865, 212960, 33672, '<td valign="top">The comp and Idea warrant a high score! If the jewlery were brighter ot there were a little more contrast I''d give it a ten.. It''s still one of my top picks for this challenge. the lighting is great.</td>', 'The comp and Idea warrant a high score! If the jewlery were brighter ot there were a little more contrast I''d give it a ten.. It''s still one of my top picks for this challenge. the lighting is great.', '2005-08-06 00:28:31.000000', NULL, 1),
