(1600460, 212688, 1570, '<td valign="top">thanks a lot for all your comments, it was so much fun shooting minnie - this is my favorite picture of the year so far... to answer some of your questions: i did this on the table which i draped with towels and moved to the very edge of the pool... i did try the glasses on her, but they were just too big... i didn''t know how she will behave in the chair, so i was totally surprised when she just sat there, smelling the flowers from time to time, that''s all... i did take several pictures, but mostly to make sure that all of the props are in the picture... as to the comments that she doesn''t look happy i might kid you back that "money does not buy happiness", but i won''t... minnie is generally a very happy dawg and a very good sport, she likes to stay by my side at all times except when playing with her best friend, 95 pound shepherd mix basia... i do agree that here she does look a little on a melancholic side but i think that her looking like that goes along with the whole ambience of relaxation I was trying to convey... the outtakes are here: "//share.shutterfly.com/share/received/welcome.sfly?fid=7bd04e61f52a41833315f89dbf2f35f7&amp;sid=9MYtGjZk1gw"<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-05-22 19:33:21.</i></td>', 'thanks a lot for all your comments, it was so much fun shooting minnie - this is my favorite picture of the year so far... to answer some of your questions: i did this on the table which i draped with towels and moved to the very edge of the pool... i did try the glasses on her, but they were just too big... i didn''t know how she will behave in the chair, so i was totally surprised when she just sat there, smelling the flowers from time to time, that''s all... i did take several pictures, but mostly to make sure that all of the props are in the picture... as to the comments that she doesn''t look happy i might kid you back that "money does not buy happiness", but i won''t... minnie is generally a very happy dawg and a very good sport, she likes to stay by my side at all times except when playing with her best friend, 95 pound shepherd mix basia... i do agree that here she does look a little on a melancholic side but i think that her looking like that goes along with the whole ambience of relaxation I was trying to convey... the outtakes are here: "//share.shutterfly.com/share/received/welcome.sfly?fid=7bd04e61f52a41833315f89dbf2f35f7&sid=9MYtGjZk1gw"', '2005-08-10 10:28:58.000000', '2012-05-22 20:33:21.000000', 0),
